<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Capelianus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 238</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Capelianus was the Roman governor of Numidia who crushed the revolt of the Gordians in 238. Loyal to the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximinus-thrax">Maximinus Thrax</a>, he marched the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legio-iii-augusta">Third Legion Augusta</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, defeated the hastily raised forces of the new emperors and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gordian-ii">Gordian II</a> in battle, after which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gordian-i">Gordian I</a> hanged himself. His victory was short-lived, as the Senate continued the revolt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p></div>
